WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.829 --> 00:00:13.191
The drought finally passed.

2
00:00:14.352 --> 00:00:19.933
The old bear, Baloo, had already taught Mowgli many things about the law of the jungle.

3
00:00:21.974 --> 00:00:24.935
Mowgli learned important lessons from the wolves too.

4
00:00:25.975 --> 00:00:29.016
Father Wolf taught Mowgli to pay attention to sounds.

5
00:00:30.308 --> 00:00:32.589
"Every sound in the jungle means something.

6
00:00:33.409 --> 00:00:37.431
Listen carefully to the rustle of the grass and the owls' song.

7
00:00:39.112 --> 00:00:41.793
The owls can tell you when danger is coming."

8
00:00:45.034 --> 00:00:49.696
Mowgli's wolf brothers showed Mowgli how to watch how other animals acted.

9
00:00:50.757 --> 00:00:53.378
Bats scratched the trees before they rested.

10
00:00:55.659 --> 00:00:58.280
Fish splashed in the pools when they were hungry.

11
00:01:00.324 --> 00:01:05.688
Meanwhile the monkeys, up in the trees, watched Mowgli all day long.

12
00:01:06.728 --> 00:01:09.310
They saw him weaving sticks to make a shelter.

13
00:01:13.513 --> 00:01:17.616
They watched him build little huts from rocks and stomp in the mud.

14
00:01:20.157 --> 00:01:23.460
Mowgli was just playing, like all children of his age.

15
00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:26.662
But the monkeys didn't know it was just play.

16
00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:29.364
So they watched his movements with awe.

17
00:01:30.676 --> 00:01:36.001
"The man cub is very wise, with so many talents," one monkey said.

18
00:01:36.021 --> 00:01:39.164
"Hey!" another monkey said.

19
00:01:39.184 --> 00:01:41.586
"Maybe he can be our leader!"

20
00:01:41.606 --> 00:01:44.609
"Yes," another added.

21
00:01:44.629 --> 00:01:49.433
"Everybody in the jungle will envy us if he's our leader.

22
00:01:50.314 --> 00:01:53.236
Let's find a way to bring him to Monkey City!"

23
00:01:56.159 --> 00:02:01.235
One hot afternoon the monkeys spotted Mowgli napping with Bagheera and Baloo.

24
00:02:01.255 --> 00:02:06.799
"This is our chance to steal the man cub," a monkey whispered.

25
00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:08.401
"Let's go!"

26
00:02:08.421 --> 00:02:12.203
A group of monkeys swooped down.

27
00:02:13.304 --> 00:02:17.327
The next thing Mowgli knew, hands were grabbing his legs and arms.

28
00:02:18.068 --> 00:02:22.872
Then the two strongest monkeys grabbed Mowgli and swung off.

29
00:02:27.692 --> 00:02:29.353
Branches scratched his face.

30
00:02:30.653 --> 00:02:31.793
Then he heard Baloo.

31
00:02:32.473 --> 00:02:36.014
The bear's loud cry woke up the entire jungle.

32
00:02:37.275 --> 00:02:41.656
The monkeys just laughed.

33
00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.577
They flew through the treetops.

34
00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:48.158
"Whoa!" Mowgli felt dizzy.

35
00:02:48.998 --> 00:02:51.159
Branches and leaves slapped his face.

36
00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:58.299
Bounding, crashing, whooping, and yelling, the whole tribe of monkeys swept through the jungle.

37
00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:01.601
"Let me go!"

38
00:03:01.982 --> 00:03:02.782
Mowgli cried.

39
00:03:03.523 --> 00:03:05.164
They were up high in the trees.

40
00:03:06.205 --> 00:03:08.747
He was terrified that the monkeys would drop him.

41
00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:13.251
Then he grew angry and started to think.

42
00:03:13.271 --> 00:03:17.374
"Baloo and Bagheera will try to find me," he thought.

43
00:03:18.795 --> 00:03:23.940
But the monkeys were traveling so fast, Mowgli's friends couldn't possibly catch up.

44
00:03:24.928 --> 00:03:27.470
How could he leave them a clue about where he was?

45
00:03:29.191 --> 00:03:30.871
It was useless to look down.

46
00:03:31.692 --> 00:03:32.933
That made Mowgli dizzy.

47
00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.094
So he looked up.

48
00:03:35.974 --> 00:03:40.937
And there, far away in the blue sky, he saw Rann, the hawk.

49
00:03:41.998 --> 00:03:45.620
Rann was flying over the jungle, searching for something to eat.

50
00:03:46.981 --> 00:03:50.022
Rann finally looked down and spotted the monkeys.

51
00:03:50.042 --> 00:03:52.684
"Hmm," he said.

52
00:03:53.924 --> 00:03:56.245
"Are those monkeys carrying something?"

53
00:03:57.505 --> 00:03:59.566
He swooped down to get a better look.

54
00:04:01.486 --> 00:04:04.947
Mowgli, of course, knew all the languages of the jungle.

55
00:04:05.648 --> 00:04:07.288
He let out a loud whistle.

56
00:04:07.308 --> 00:04:12.110
"Huh?" Surprised, Rann whistled back.

57
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:14.330
"Mowgli? Is that you?"

58
00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:17.971
"Rann! Follow me!"

59
00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:20.052
Mowgli shouted to the hawk.

60
00:04:20.728 --> 00:04:23.910
"Then tell Baloo and Bagheera where I am!"

61
00:04:30.953 --> 00:04:34.776
had climbed the tree after Mowgli, but the monkeys were too fast.

62
00:04:36.837 --> 00:04:39.678
Then the thin branches snapped beneath his weight.

63
00:04:40.479 --> 00:04:43.720
The panther slipped down, his claws full of bark.

64
00:04:45.001 --> 00:04:47.362
Baloo had set off at a clumsy run.

65
00:04:47.382 --> 00:04:50.504
"Come on, Bagheera!"

66
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.582
"You couldn't catch a wounded cow at that pace," Bagheera said.

67
00:04:55.602 --> 00:04:58.684
"Sit still and let's make a plan."

68
00:04:59.645 --> 00:05:01.306
Baloo dropped to the ground.

69
00:05:01.326 --> 00:05:03.727
"This is terrible!"

70
00:05:05.568 --> 00:05:07.409
he moaned, rolling around.

71
00:05:07.429 --> 00:05:12.432
"Stop curling up like a porcupine," Bagheera snapped.

72
00:05:12.452 --> 00:05:15.134
"We need to figure out what to do."

73
00:05:15.154 --> 00:05:18.676
"But Baloo gulped.

74
00:05:19.532 --> 00:05:21.679
"But Mowgli might be dead by now!"
